{
  "_why": "Role track for WELDING, authored under docs/profiling/role-pack-authoring-guide.md as Batch 2's fabrication pack. fam_welding stays the generic ISCO-unit-7212 interview and is NOT touched; this pack belongs to fam_welding_trade, which binds the NCO welding occupations directly (job_domain specificity 50 beats unit 40), so a production welder gets welding depth and every other worker in 7212 — the plumber-welder, the brazier, the solderer — keeps the interview they have today. The ids differ (qp_welding_trade / fam_welding_trade) rather than this pack overwriting qp_welding, because assertRegistryIsCoherent rejects a duplicate packId and descriptorForPack would otherwise start answering for the generic pack's workers.",
  "_scope": "ARC, MIG/MAG, TIG, GAS CUTTING AND SPOT, on structural and sheet fabrication -- the whole trade, not one process. welding_process is asked of everyone rather than used as a router, because a man who runs a rod set on site and a CO2 machine in the shop is one welder with two processes, not two roles. The level ladder (Helper / Welder / Certified Welder) is asked as welder_level so the sheet can print '{Role} -- {Level}' from a fact the worker STATED; RoleFormDescriptor.levelLadder is the list this question offers, and nothing infers a rung from tenure.",
  "_depth": "THE TIER GATE IS welding_experience, asked FIRST, and it is WELDER.tenureQuestionKey. It cannot be experience_years from qp_universal: phase order runs occupation_specific BEFORE universal_tail, so the universal answer does not exist yet when these items are selected -- gating on it is permanently false. Its options carry value_number ONLY. pack-registry.service.ts resolves valueText ?? valueNumber ?? valueBool, so one stray value_text would make the captured answer a STRING, compare() would refuse to order it against a number and return null, and EVERY gte/lte below would evaluate false forever, silently. Every predicate here uses the contract shape {op, left:{field}, right:{const}} -- the older {op, args:[...]} shape is #776, the defect that left two qp_welding questions unasked for the life of that pack, and this is the trade it was found in.",
  "_budget": "MAX_ENGINE_ASKS is 28 and qp_universal spends 8. Tier 0 is 8 items (8 + 8 = 16), tier 1 (welding_experience >= 2) adds 3 (19), tier 2 (>= 5) adds 4 (23) -- five asks of headroom against the ceiling. The three fresher items are gated welding_experience <= 0, so a senior never sees them and a fresher, who fails both gte gates by construction, tops out at 16 + 3 = 19. The tiers are mutually exclusive, which is why the fresher branch costs the senior nothing. 18 items, 0 of them duplicating qp_universal's primary_trade / experience_years / current_city / salary_expected / preferred_locations / availability / education / shift_preference.",
  "_sheet": "SECTION B IS READ OFF THE RATIFIED WELDER REFERENCE RESUME, not invented. Its nine rows are Processes, Equipment, Electrodes/wire, Materials, Positions, Inspection, Plate thickness, Drawings and Sector worked, and every one has a question here that fills it. Plate thickness is a BANDED single_select rather than a free number: the sheet prints '3 mm - 25 mm plate', which is a band, and a banded chip keeps a low-literacy worker tapping instead of typing while avoiding answer_type 'number', which has no Flutter widget. The four tier-2 items (joint_type, machine_setting, weld_defect, fabrication_work) deliberately have NO sheet row -- the ratified page has none and this pack does not invent one; they are matching data in worker_attributes, which is where trade depth with no printed slot belongs.",
  "_keys": "NO DIGITS IN ANY question_key OR option_key. Both regexes are ^[a-z_]+$, and slugKey REFUSES a key with a digit at runtime even where the corpus validator historically let it through -- one such key makes the whole pack unparseable. So the positions are flat/horizontal/vertical/overhead and the consumables are e_six_zero_one_three / e_seven_zero_one_eight / er_seventy_s_six. THE LABEL KEEPS THE REAL SHOP-FLOOR TEXT ('1G flat', 'E6013 rod'), because the label is the worker's answer of record; only the key is letters.",
  "pack_id": "qp_welding_trade",
  "version": 1,
  "family_id": "fam_welding_trade",
  "locale": "hi-IN",
  "status": "active",
  "review_note": "Drafted for owner review (Prakash). Shop-floor vocabulary NOT yet corrected by a practising welder -- see docs/registers/trade-content-ratification.md.",
  "_fresher": "Guideline section 11 #1: a fresher's Zone 4 is training, trade test, machines used in the ITI workshop and project work, and the History heading never renders empty. These three items are the ask half; resume-fresher-rows.ts, fed by this role's descriptor, is the render half. The KEYS are read literally by that file and must not be renamed; only the workshop VOCABULARY is trade-specific, and a welder's ITI workshop holds welding sets, not lathes.",
